&lt;p&gt;P-1533&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Databricks, we are passionate about enabling data teams to solve the world&#39;s toughest problems — from making the next mode of transportation a reality to accelerating the development of medical breakthroughs. We do this by building and running the world&#39;s best data and AI infrastructure platform so our customers can use deep data insights to improve their business.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Networking Infrastructure is a core part of the platform that powers all our data and AI products. The platform also powers key enterprise security features used by customers across all our products to build connectivity solutions to cloud resources and prevent data exfiltration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an experienced &lt;strong&gt;Sr. Staff Software Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; with deep networking expertise to help shape the future of Databricks’ &lt;strong&gt;Networking Infrastructure&lt;/strong&gt;. As one of the early members of the rapidly growing Bangalore site, you will play a critical role in &lt;strong&gt;defining the technical vision and architecture&lt;/strong&gt; for next-generation network connectivity &amp;amp; observability services that will power &amp;amp; manage &lt;strong&gt;millions of VMs across multiple clouds&lt;/strong&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will &lt;strong&gt;own and drive the design of large-scale connectivity platforms&lt;/strong&gt; that form the backbone between Databricks’ &lt;strong&gt;control plane and compute plane&lt;/strong&gt;. These platforms are foundational to improving the &lt;strong&gt;scalability, reliability, and efficiency&lt;/strong&gt; of our compute infrastructure, while enabling more intelligent and cost-effective use of cloud resources.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will operate at an &lt;strong&gt;org-wide level&lt;/strong&gt;, setting technical direction, leading complex cross-team initiatives, and mentoring senior engineers. You’ll work closely with product management, operations, and partner engineering teams to translate long-term business goals into &lt;strong&gt;durable, extensible networking systems&lt;/strong&gt;. This role requires both &lt;strong&gt;hands-on technical leadership&lt;/strong&gt; and the ability to influence architecture and execution across teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a unique opportunity for a &lt;strong&gt;senior technical leader&lt;/strong&gt; who enjoys working in ambiguous problem spaces and is motivated by solving &lt;strong&gt;novel, multi-cloud distributed systems challenges at massive scale&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What we look for:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years of production level experience in one of: Rust, Java, Scala, C++, or similar language&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience developing large-scale distributed systems from scratch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on a SaaS platform or with Service-Oriented Architectures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with cloud networking, kubernetes, infrastructure automation languages like terraform, cloudformation, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Databricks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
